{
  "description": "Cross-host tree-diff golden family (Phase 557 tail). Pins (before, after) -> canonical TreeOp op-script for the structural diff producer shipped in every headless host (go diff/diff.go, rs src/diff, py fuaran_py.ops.diff), the sibling of the F# TreeOpDiff engine. Every entry's op-script was GENERATED by running the actual shipped producers, not hand-authored. Two sections: 'goldens' are pairs where go, rs and py produce the IDENTICAL canonical op-script (the common structural surface: identical trees -> empty script; a changed root id -> ReplaceRoot(after), the only op that may swap the root id) - every host asserts Diff(before, after) == ops AND Apply(ops, before) == after. 'divergent' pairs are where the producers legitimately differ in GRANULARITY (never in correctness - all satisfy the round-trip law): go and rs take the whole-node-replace strategy (RemoveNode + InsertChild at the changed node's seat), while py refines to a granular field op (UpdateProp); each carries a per-host expected op-script under 'hosts' so every host still certifies against the shared file, and the divergence is documented in the entry's 'description'. The 'divergent' section also encodes the Modal/ScrollArea-interior case (modal-interior-change / scrollarea-interior-change): Modal and ScrollArea carry a 'children' field but are NOT among the six layout kinds the go and py apply engines address structurally, whereas the rs apply engine DOES address them - so a diff INSIDE one escalates three ways, all round-trip-correct: go whole-node-replaces the container at its seat (RemoveNode+InsertChild), py takes the EditNode floor at the container, and rs recurses through it to whole-node-replace the interior leaf. Hence a 'divergent' entry's per-host scripts can differ in BOTH shape (EditNode vs RemoveNode+InsertChild vs UpdateProp) and depth (which node is replaced), never in correctness.",
